 4058 2ABB ~            ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 4059 2ABB ~            ; Shifts of DE:HL by the count in BC. A count at or above the width gives zero, or all sign bits
 4060 2ABB ~            ; for an arithmetic shift -- which is what shifting by one less than the width gives, so there the
 4061 2ABB ~            ; count is clamped rather than special-cased. In registers: eight places at a time by moving
 4062 2ABB ~            ; the bytes, then a bit a step -- ADD HL,HL and two rotations through A to
