 5588 2BEB ~
 5589 2BEB ~            ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 5590 2BEB ~            ; __x80_dpass8: the same for a divisor d of 1..255, held as B = d * 128 in BC, -B in DE
 5591 2BEB ~            ; (__x80_dsetup8). HL is a remainder below d times 256 plus the next byte of the dividend; returns
 5592 2BEB ~            ; the byte of HL / d in A, and the remainder in H, with L zero -- where the next byte goes. The
 5593 2BEB ~            ; first step takes B off without doubling; the last doubling puts the remainder, which is 128
 5594 2BEB ~            ; times too large, into H.
